From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] ui-egui: selection handles and a long-press action bar for a finger

Phase 6 WP5 (docs/phase6/PLAN.md section 4). With a finger, a text selection shows two round handles under its ends; dragging one resizes the selection (the other end stays, handles may cross, the finger is offset so it never covers the text, the page edge scrolls on as for a mouse drag) and lifting resets the IME (Gboard counts corrections from the text since the caret last moved). A long press still selects the word (0004) but opens a bar of Cut / Copy / Paste / Select All / more instead of the desktop context menu (egui reports the same press as a secondary click); "more" opens the usual context menu at the caret. The formatting mini toolbar stands down for a finger. A press on something floating above the page (the bar, a menu) is no longer carried out on the page underneath. All of it is in the new touch_select.rs; canvas.rs gets call lines. Mouse behaviour is unchanged: nothing is routed or drawn unless the last pointer was a finger.
